Build order: X libraries, before Mesa 25.3.6 (mesa-core/Mesa) and before the
top-level Xrandr recipe (the xrandr client links against this library).
Ported from the canonical GoboLinux recipe LibXRandR/1.5.2 (Lucas C. Villa
Real, 08 Feb 2020). URL, file_size and file_md5 are identical to upstream and
to the tarball behind the ISO's /Programs/LibXRandR/1.5.2.
Why it is needed: Mesa 25.3.6 sets with_xlib_lease from the 'xlib-lease'
feature, whose require() condition is (platforms include x11) and
system_has_kms_drm. Our recipe builds -Dplatforms=x11,wayland on a DRM/KMS
system, so the condition holds and meson.build does
  dep_xrandr = dependency('xrandr')
with no required:false -- a missing xrandr.pc aborts configure. (This is the
same probe described in mesa-core/Mesa/25.3.6/Resources/BuildInformation.)
Name collision warning: the dependency name is xrandr.pc, so the package is
LibXRandR, but the xrandr CLI client is the separate top-level Recipes/Xrandr
(xrandr-1.5.2.tar.xz, recipe_type=configure). Both are needed; the client links
libXrandr.so.2 from this package.
The upstream URL form was rewritten from
https://x.org/archive/individual/lib/... to
https://xorg.freedesktop.org/archive/individual/lib/... because the old
www.x.org/releases/individual/lib/ path 404s for 1.5.2 (verified 2026-10-18).
Build deps: xrandr.pc declares `Requires: xproto randrproto >= 1.5` (both from
XorgProto) and `Requires.private: x11 xext xrender` -- xorgproto.pc 2024.1,
LibX11 1.8.13 (our recipe), LibXext 1.3.4 and LibXrender 0.9.10 are all
installed Programs.
Output: lib/libXrandr.so.2.x.y (+ libXrandr.so.2, libXrandr.so),
include/X11/extensions/Xrandr.h, lib/pkgconfig/xrandr.pc, share/man/man3/*.
